      "lineNbr": 188,
      "author": {
        "id": 5255
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-24T18:46:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t remember - how does libwebp handle a different width and height per frame? We should do something reasonable and consistent. This means documenting in the header file and writing tests. (It doesn\u0027t guarantee that we\u0027ll follow it if/when we add support for another format, but it gives us something to start with!)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 187,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 188,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "e3ce613f91acf7e58a3114d04c7376ea99d7e1b9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ce5b3b49_5800d638",
        "filename": "src/images/SkWebpEncoder.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 188,
      "author": {
        "id": 5920
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-24T19:13:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I don\u0027t remember - how does libwebp handle a different width and height per frame? We should do something reasonable and consistent. This means documenting in the header file and writing tests. (It doesn\u0027t guarantee that we\u0027ll follow it if/when we add support for another format, but it gives us something to start with!)\n\nA frame can be \u003c\u003d to the canvas size in webp. offsets are snapped to even values.",
      "parentUuid": "807a88c2_562ece88",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 187,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 188,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "e3ce613f91acf7e58a3114d04c7376ea99d7e1b9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8270d7ef_e246a6e5",
        "filename": "src/images/SkWebpEncoder.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 188,
      "author": {
        "id": 5255
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-24T21:12:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the details! We should document how this is handled in the Skia API. (In `SkWebPEncoder.h` - I still think `Frame` should move to `SkEncoder`, but this may be handled differently per encoder.)\n\nThis also brings up that a `Frame` should have offset values.\n\nWe might also want a way to specify the canvas size. One option, implicit here, is that the canvas is the size of the first image. But I think that would limit some things that the encoder would otherwise allow us to do.\n\nAnd what should happen if a frame doesn\u0027t fit within the canvas? I think that should be an error.",
      "parentUuid": "ce5b3b49_5800d638",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 187,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 188,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "e3ce613f91acf7e58a3114d04c7376ea99d7e1b9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1620c01a_8ff8d6dc",
        "filename": "src/images/SkWebpEncoder.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 188,
      "author": {
        "id": 5920
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-24T22:02:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Thanks for the details! We should document how this is handled in the Skia API. (In `SkWebPEncoder.h` - I still think `Frame` should move to `SkEncoder`, but this may be handled differently per encoder.)\n\u003e \n\u003e This also brings up that a `Frame` should have offset values.\n\u003e \n\u003e We might also want a way to specify the canvas size. One option, implicit here, is that the canvas is the size of the first image. But I think that would limit some things that the encoder would otherwise allow us to do.\n\u003e \n\nI think that is limiting if you wanted to define a large canvas and use the background color to cover all but a section of it for instance.\n\n\u003e And what should happen if a frame doesn\u0027t fit within the canvas? I think that should be an error.\n\nThat makes sense to me.",
      "parentUuid": "8270d7ef_e246a6e5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 187,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 188,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "e3ce613f91acf7e58a3114d04c7376ea99d7e1b9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "086c2739_702f93bb",
        "filename": "src/images/SkWebpEncoder.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 188,
      "author": {
        "id": 19204
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-25T00:39:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I do not think libwebp support customized offset for each frames (James correct me if I am wrong), The canvas sizes are directly specified in WebPAnimEncoderNew and when adding frames, if the sizes not match the frame will be dropped[1].\n\nI do see there are options to set background color and loop limit[2], and customize lossy/lossless for per frame[3](do we want to expose these options in the Skia API?).\n\n[1]https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/libwebp/src/src/mux/anim_encode.c;l\u003d1378\n[2]https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/libwebp/src/src/webp/mux.h;l\u003d281\n[3]https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/libwebp/src/src/webp/mux.h;l\u003d437",
      "parentUuid": "1620c01a_8ff8d6dc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 187,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 188,
        "endChar": 37
